description:
FILED s535a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08) from a span-port probe (scratch/s535a/pr/p20.pl).  The base 06a4b8ba was SILENTLY wrong; since s535a the file is REFUSED loudly (the span pass sees the use and cannot rewrite it).

REPRODUCER (probed vs perl 5.40.3):

    my $p = "FILE";
    package Foo;
    use feature 'signatures'; no warnings; sub f ($q = $p) { "f=$q" }
    print f(), "\n";

perl:          f=FILE
base 06a4b8ba: f=            (SILENT WRONG: the default read $Foo::p)
s535a:         Parser2 TODO: my-lexical 'p' (canon $p) spans a package boundary

WHY: with the feature pragma on the sub's OWN line PPI hands the signature over as ONE Token::Prototype (#455), whose text holds the default `$p`; the binder reads the default's uses (Binder::_proto_params), so the span pass knows `$p` crosses into section Foo -- but a one-token signature has no Symbol to rename, so the promotion refuses (the capture promoter's own rule for the same spelling, 'signature default in an unrewritable Token::Prototype') and the checker refuses the file.

FIX DIRECTION: rewrite the default's variable inside the Prototype token's TEXT when every `$p` the token spells is the same binding (the binder's per-token answer), or re-parse such a signature as a Structure::Signature once the feature is known to be in force (the #455 boundary).  Rare: needs the pragma and the sub on one line plus a default naming a file lexical across a package switch.

=== DONE (s536e) ===
FIXED (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08, generation v2-12900; commit 23baa13b).  `Pl/Parser2.pm` `_rename_in_proto_defaults($proto, $old, $new)` renames a variable inside the DEFAULTS of a one-token signature (Token::Prototype, #455): each part's default re-parsed as a fragment (Pl::Parser::fragment_doc) so a Symbol, a `${x}` brace and interpolated text follow and a single-quoted string does not; never a parameter NAME; it stops at the part that declares the name itself (a later default sees that parameter, Binder::_proto_params' `%left`); only where the token IS a signature (head_is_signature).  Called by the span scalar rewrite (`_span_rewrite_stmt`), the span container loop and `_rewrite_var_uses` -- so the capture promoter's mangle and the `our` requalifiers (#475's `_requalify_spanning_ours`, the block requalifier) rewrite it too; the two refusals ('a use in an unrewritable Token::Prototype', 'signature default in an unrewritable Token::Prototype') are DELETED.  Probed (scratch/s536e/pr/m4*.pl): the reproducer, several defaults incl. `scalar(@v)` / `"<$p>"` / `'$p'`, a parameter named like the lexical (`($p = $p, $q = $p)`), a `$h{k}` default, a default + a body write, the capture promoter's mangle (`my $p; { my $p }` + a signature sub: was "file lexical 'p' captured by sub f"), an `our $t` across `package A;` read by a default (was silently `$A::t`) -- tree = perl.  Guard span-binder-01.t rows 33-35 (fail on the base).  Gate-SET identical.
